{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1513927-help-with-encounter-ideas","id":1513927,"title":"help with encounter ideas","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-06-05T02:44:05-07:00","id":1513927,"title":"help with encounter ideas","content":"im going to start a campaign with a city on fire [ancient rome], the players will be in it.<br /> <br /> the first few sessions will be them dealing with their touchstones and the fires. but i want to up the drama, and have the entrances to the catacombs blocked so they have to spend 4 days above ground while the city burns.<br /> <br /> what i dont want to do is just keep having their touchstones in danger for the whole time [say 1 session per night], but other than a riot or two, im at a loss as to what could be fun and interesting nightly encounters with a back drop of a city on fire.<br /> <br /> any help would be weclomed","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1637-zen","name":"zen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-05T10:39:56-07:00","id":1513959,"title":"","content":"Taking advantage of the fire, the Strix make their move against the Camarilla and all the clans","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">Organizer for the Dead Gamers Society: The So Cal World of Darkness Meetup. </span><a href=\"http://www.meetup.com/Dead-Gamers-Society/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.meetup.com/Dead-Gamers-Society/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/85-drumheller","name":"Drumheller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar85_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-05T19:04:32-07:00","id":1513983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drumheller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1513927-help-with-encounter-ideas?p=1513959#post1513959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Taking advantage of the fire, the Strix make their move against the Camarilla and all the clans</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe it's just me, but i feel throwing the Strix gunning for revenge when the game is just begining might be &quot;jumping the gun&quot; a little too much, letting them get a feel of their Requiems and how undead existence in Rome is different from modern times might be better for a first. Not to mention the Strix are not the greatest fans of flames either.<br /> <br /> But back to the basics, i can see ways to explore the matter of the fire, going from the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marcus_Licinius_Crassus#Rise_to_power_and_wealth\" target=\"_blank\">mundane</a> to the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vesta_(mythology)\" target=\"_blank\">religious</a>, if not outright <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Pyrokinesis\" target=\"_blank\">spiritual/supernatural</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-06T03:20:40-07:00","id":1513999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1513927-help-with-encounter-ideas#post1513927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">im going to start a campaign with a city on fire [ancient rome], the players will be in it.</div> </div> </div> </div>In what period happens the fire and how big it is? A Rome post-civil wars in the cusp of empire with either Caesar or Augustus will be quite different from one in the nights of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nero#Great_Fire_of_Rome\" target=\"_blank\">Nero</a>, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Year_of_the_Four_Emperors\" target=\"_blank\">the year of Four Emperors</a> just after it, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crisis_of_the_Third_Century\" target=\"_blank\">the 3rd century</a> or <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Constantine_the_Great#Constantine_adopts_the_Greek_letters_Chi_Rho_for_Christ&#39;s_initials\" target=\"_blank\">the ascension of christianism to power</a>, both in character and geography, due to construction and destruction of buildings, cults, families and alliances through the epochs. Taking a little time to jot down some bits of info help you to make things more more colorful and specific could be good.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1513927-help-with-encounter-ideas#post1513927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the first few sessions will be them dealing with their touchstones and the fires. but i want to up the drama, and have the entrances to the catacombs blocked so they have to spend 4 days above ground while the city burns.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, why would they be? The reason can be important since some of the kindred above might think of foul play, justified or not, others might try to open them by force consequences be damned and so on. Also, it's good to remember that <i>the living</i> have also made extensive use of the catacombs of Rome through the ages, what can bring all kinds of opportunities and trouble depending on the kinds of people, circunstances and so on.<br /> <br /> One more thing - touchstones might not be kindred, but it doesn't have to mean they are incapable or weak. Loved ones can run the whole gamut from nearly defenseless poor orphaned infant child or grandchild to roman legionaries like the main characters in HBO's Rome or entrenched members of the senate, legions and state bureaucracy.<br /> <br /> They have talents, skills, interests, passions and ambitions of their own - they can find themselves in danger by accident and ill fate, but they can also endanger themselves <i>of their own volition</i> by putting crazy plans, vengeances, conspiracies and more in action amidst the chaos. Have no shame in exploiting the hell out of this.<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 06-06-2023, 06:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-06T03:38:01-07:00","id":1514000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> n what period happens the fire and how big it is </div> </div> </div>the period is going to be Nero eras, so it starts with the fire.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well, why would they be </div> </div> </div>in the paragraph about the fires in RfR, it says that the entrances were blocked, and i liked the idea that the players have to survive outside, no haven no allies etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> they can find themselves in danger by accident and ill fate, but they can also endanger themselves </div> </div> </div>and i agree about the touchstones, but i just dont want to over do the, put the touchstones in danger all the time thing, it is one of my pet peves about the touchstone system. the: lets put them in constant life threathening situations to create drama. i dont mind doing it now and then when it makes sense, but id rather they were more normal human encounters as a counter balance to the strange of the vampire society. ok i know what im trying to say, but dont seem to be able to put it into words lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1637-zen","name":"zen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-07T07:51:57-07:00","id":1514114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1513927-help-with-encounter-ideas?p=1514000#post1514000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the period is going to be Nero eras, so it starts with the fire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Great choice, quite evocative tragedy that has inspired iconic works of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quo_Vadis_(novel)\" target=\"_blank\">literature</a> and cinema. <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Great_Fire_of_Rome\" target=\"_blank\">This</a> can provide a a solid summary to help you set up things and cook up a basic timeline and enviroment for the PCs to deal with.<br /> <br /> (The part on separate stories that would later circulate about the Nero and his actions during or after the incident can provide some nice fodder for subplots, wild rumours to investigate, clamp down or fan even hotter, depending on one's agendas and loyalties)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1513927-help-with-encounter-ideas?p=1514000#post1514000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">in the paragraph about the fires in RfR, it says that the entrances were blocked, and i liked the idea that the players have to survive outside, no haven no allies etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>That in itself is interesting, because it raises all kinds of problems and later questions - for starters, it means there will be a bunch of other kindred of all ages, classes and clans who are also blocked out in the surface, where you are all easy targets for the flames or frenzy at the worst of times. They also have touchstones, allies, rivals and other things to worry about. They could provide all kinds of additional help or trouble depending on circunstances - a frenzied Mekhet neonate is an issue, but a frenzied Daeva or Nosferatu elder can be a cconsiderably more threatening one.<br /> <br /> Some will accept their bad fortune and deal with it as they can in the ensuing nights (according to some accounts only after <i><b>six days</b></i> was the fire was brought under control - but before the damage could be assessed, <i>the fire reignited</i> and <i><b>burned for another three days</b></i>), while others might grow desperate and paranoid, trying to find ways to get into the Necropolis, by either trickery, seeking alternate entrances or forming a crazed mob to force one or more entrances open.<br /> <br /> Plus, there will be those who will raise all kinds of accusations on the Senex, Julii, Augurs, foreigners (or whoever you can think of) over the handling of the situation, much like the living will do with Nero, might be said.<br /> <br /> None of that going into the fact the dead are far from the only people with strange powers, urges or limitations that might hide amidst the ranks of the masses - local werewolves, mages and more might have worries and priorities of their own, not to mention the ever-looming possibility of hunters getting in the way of any supernaturals that get a little too unruly amidst the general disorder.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1513927-help-with-encounter-ideas?p=1514000#post1514000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and i agree about the touchstones, but i just dont want to over do the, put the touchstones in danger all the time thing, it is one of my pet peves about the touchstone system. the: lets put them in constant life threathening situations to create drama. i dont mind doing it now and then when it makes sense, but id rather they were more normal human encounters as a counter balance to the strange of the vampire society. ok i know what im trying to say, but dont seem to be able to put it into words lol.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think i see what you mean but you have a whole city in danger of going up in flames - that's very much a disaster movie terrain, danger will be the norm <i>for everybody</i>, the touchstones are simply those in whose continued well-being the PCs have a very personal stake upon.<br /> <br /> Knowing one's player's and experimenting with the handling is the key - a loved one or relative getting kidnapped, bumping into a near-frenzied vampire or surrounded in one's own home by a &quot;<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vigiles\" target=\"_blank\">fire brigade</a>&quot; who are pretty much a gang of arsonists is one kind of danger.<br /> <br /> Now, a loved one invading the home of a hated moneylender along with the neighborhood watch to gank the bastard, or invading a patrician or equestrian's house to &quot;disappear&quot; with that worthy's slave concubine he has a secret affair with, well, whole different kind of danger depending on one's point of view. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, six nights of fire - set up a timeline for your own reference/convenience and prepare your players for potentially much trouble with finding places to sleep safely, where nobody is really safe anymore.<br /> <br /> Hope this helps a bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 06-07-2023, 11:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-09T15:08:26-07:00","id":1514341,"title":"","content":"Just one problem; at the time of Nero, the catacombs weren't really constructed; they were constructed in the 2nd-century, AD, onward, as Christians disliked being cremated. <br /> <br /> Also, since Rome has been occupied since around 900BC, there can be pre-Roman tombs like, Etruscan tombs that, perhaps, can be inter-connected or have been dug a bit to connect. Who's to say the Christians didn't simply erase the Etruscan writings with their own writings and call it their catacombs?<br /> <br /> And Rome was built in a swamp, so, some areas, underground, should be very wet and or flooded. And unlike most ancient-cities, which had a dedicated area for the upper-class, by the time of the Empire, the Emperor took all the good land for his palaces, so, the upper-class (Senators), in Rome had to live spread out. This means, slums could be a small-neighborhood right next to a wealthy villa.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}